      "derived": [
        {
          "id": "AC-073",
          "reason": "The story names the summary's elements but not their copy; the engineering reference requires all user-facing copy to come from Strapi except the fallback, as AC-008 and AC-040 do for the earlier steps, and missing copy must be invalid content (P3)."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-075",
          "reason": "The story says the person views the terms but not how; the design reference places a terms link below the call to action and requires keyboard operation, visible focus and no traps, so the dialog's focus, closing and scrolling must be stated."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-077",
          "reason": "The story has no loading, unavailable, missing or duplicated terms case; principle P3, the architecture (terms are read with the country's content) and the gap checklist (Strapi unavailable, content not published) require controlled states, as AC-015 to AC-017 and AC-059 do."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-079",
          "reason": "The story does not say what leaves the browser to pay; principles P4 and P5, the engineering reference (personal data is not logged) and AC-026 and AC-046 require the minimum: country and plan only, nothing stored or logged by the stateless endpoint."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-082",
          "reason": "The story needs terms and a payment endpoint but says nothing about access; principle P4 and the architecture limit the public role to read actions on wizard content types plus the two custom endpoints, with no token in the browser."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-086",
          "reason": "The story does not say what happens when the person returns to earlier steps after paying; without a rule the person could pay the same quote twice or lose the confirmation, and AC-020 and AC-053 keep earlier steps navigable."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-087",
          "reason": "The story ends at the confirmation and does not say how a person quotes again in the same tab; the wizard data is kept per tab (AC-023), so without an explicit action the paid quote would stay on every visit."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-089",
          "reason": "The story does not cover reloading or leaving the summary, nor leaving while a payment is processed; the gap checklist requires stating reload and navigation, and CHG-001's leave confirmation (AC-033, AC-034) needs a statement for this step, as AC-057 gives for the plan step."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-090",
          "reason": "The story has no accessibility criteria; principle P6 and the design reference require programmatic names, associations, announced states and an automated scan in every state."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-091",
          "reason": "The story has no accessibility criteria; the design reference requires keyboard-only completion with visible focus and no traps, checked in every user interface review."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-092",
          "reason": "The story has no responsive criteria; the design reference sets the reference widths, reflow to 320 px without horizontal scrolling and the minimum target size."
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-093",
          "reason": "The story has no motion criteria; the design reference requires respecting the reduced-motion preference."
        }
      ]
    },
